module engine where

-- structural-dispatch Phase 4a — the structural subtype-match body + the ⊆-arm
-- universe-view. The PORT of the editor's browser-side `typeMatches`
-- (expression-runner/index.tsx) into `.fenel`, UPGRADED to genuine subtype
-- precision at refined leaves via the SHIPPED `set:decideSubset`. This is
-- structural-dispatch's first real `decideSubset` consumer (roadmap D3).
--
-- `typeSubsumes have want` decides "can a value of return type `have` be used
-- where `want` is expected" — i.e. `have <: want`. It recurses structurally over
-- the marshalled `TraversalType` (the `$`-key barrier: the seam marshals each
-- type via `marshalTraversalType`, the body reads the ADT) and, at a
-- `$refined`-vs-`$refined` leaf, consults `set:decideSubset` over the two
-- refinement `SetExpr`s (carried opaquely on `TtRefined.set`, Phase-4a marshal
-- extension). The matched-set fold `functionsMatchingReturn` is the ⊆-arm view
-- the editor's `FunctionPicker` consumes in-process (replacing `typeMatches`).
--
-- The two deltas over a faithful `typeMatches` port (audit §2):
--   (A) a type-VARIABLE in the EXPECTED (`want`) type accepts ANY `have` — the
--       polymorphic-slot accept (`typeMatches` had no type-var case ⇒ a
--       polymorphic expected type filtered everything out).
--   (B) both `$refined` ⇒ `set:decideSubset`: `Just b ⇒ b` (a genuine ⊆
--       decision); `Nothing` (undecided / out-of-fragment / solver fence) ⇒ fall
--       through to base congruence. So a refined leaf EXCLUDES only on a genuine
--       refutation (`Just false`) — the UX-honest "include-with-no-claim" default
--       for a picker (audit §2). Solver fences are flagged-not-built: an
--       out-of-fragment refinement returns `Nothing` ⇒ the candidate is KEPT, no
--       false exclusion ⇒ no `solver-extension` obligation forced.
--
-- DOCUMENTED coarsening (audit §3): List / Result ELEMENT congruence drops to
-- constructor-level (both-array / both-variant ⇒ match) — `typeMatches` recursed
-- the List `elem`; reconstructing it from the marshalled `TtOpaque→TtMu→
-- TtVariant(Cons).head` chain is brittle for a UX picker filter. UX-safe
-- over-inclusion; precise element congruence is a recorded tail. Maybe inner
-- recursion IS kept (cheap, the brief's named congruence test).
--
-- List iteration is the engine-body idiom (`head`/`tail` Maybe-returning natives
-- + `appendItem`; the array-repr List does not pattern-match Nil/Cons). The
-- marshalled records use PLAIN keys (no `$`-prefix), so `f.id`/`f.returnType`
-- read directly. `hasCaseNamed` is reused from `universe-views.fenel` (the same
-- `module engine` union).

-- ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- typeSubsumes — the structural subtype matcher. have <: want?
-- ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

-- typeSubsumes — the picker-view collapse of the shared `subsetW` core
-- (containment.fenel, Step 2). `subsetW True` reproduces this fold's former
-- standalone recursion arm-for-arm (the var-accept, the refined-leaf base-
-- congruence fall-through, the constructor-level composite coarsening); the
-- `Bool` collapse is NOT total (type-substrate P1(a.5) correction — this used to
-- read "`subsetW True` always returns a `Just`, so the `Nothing → True` default
-- is unreachable", and that is false: `subsetWK`'s want-side complement arm
-- calls `ttDisjoint` with NO picker flag, so a picker subset against a `¬X` want
-- rides the SOUND disjoint face, which abstains freely. The default IS reached,
-- and the P1(a.5) picker cells survived that phase's fail-closes because each
-- P1(a.5) movement was `Just true` → `Nothing`, which this default maps back to
-- `True`. That is a phase-specific observation, not an admission-monotonicity
-- law: P1(a.6)'s exact-Maybe M4 has a live `null` witness for an opposite
-- definite and its flagless transit is `proved-refute-exclude`, while its direct
-- picker branch remains unchanged. Pinned in the P1(a.5) and P1(a.6) focused
-- files). The retired
-- `tsSameKind` / `tsRefinedSubset` / `tsMaybeCongruent` are subsumed by the
-- core's `ssSameKind` / `ssRefined` / `ssMaybeCongruent`.
@label "Type subsumes"
@description "structural-dispatch Phase 4a / containment Step 2 / type-substrate P1(a.5–a.6) — `typeSubsumes have want` decides `have <: want` (can a value of return type `have` be used where `want` is expected) over the marshalled TraversalType. The picker-view of the containment relation's subset core: typeSubsumes = collapse(subsetW True) (Nothing → True — REACHABLE, correcting the previous \"unreachable since picker mode is total\": `subsetWK`'s want-side complement arm calls `ttDisjoint` with no picker flag, so a picker subset against a `¬X` want rides the SOUND disjoint face and can return Nothing, which this collapse then maps to True). P1(a.5)'s changed cells all moved Just true → Nothing and therefore kept their picker answers, but that is not a general admission-monotonicity law: P1(a.6)'s exact-Maybe M4 is a live-null-witnessed opposite definite whose flagless transit is `proved-refute-exclude`, with the direct picker route unchanged. A type-variable in `want` accepts any `have`; refined/opaque layers are transparent; at a `$refined`-vs-`$refined` leaf it consults the SHIPPED `set:decideSubset`, an undecided leaf falling through to base congruence (the picker's UX-honest default); named leaves match nominally; Maybe recurses on its inner; record/variant/arrow/map/tuple match at constructor level; tagged recurses on the phantom. The editor's FunctionPicker ⊆-arm; the precise sibling is `engine:subset` (= subsetW False)."
@tags "engine" "structural-dispatch" "subtype" "universe-views" "containment"
typeSubsumes : (have: TraversalType) -> (want: TraversalType) -> Bool
typeSubsumes have want =
  case subsetW true have want of
    Just b -> b
    Nothing -> true

-- ── classification + accessors over the marshalled TraversalType ────────────

@label "type-subsumes: tsKind"
@description "structural-dispatch Phase 4a — the head kind of a marshalled TraversalType as a String tag: var / refined / opaque / named / variant / mu / record / arrow / map / tuple / tagged / other. Internal classifier for typeSubsumes."
@tags "engine" "internal" "structural-dispatch" "subtype"
@category "engine-internal"
tsKind : (t: a) -> String
tsKind t = case t of
  TtVar -> "var"
  TtRefined {} -> "refined"
  TtOpaque {} -> "opaque"
  TtNamed {} -> "named"
  TtVariant {} -> "variant"
  TtMu {} -> "mu"
  TtRecord {} -> "record"
  TtArrow {} -> "arrow"
  TtMap {} -> "map"
  TtTuple {} -> "tuple"
  TtTagged {} -> "tagged"
  TtUnit -> "unit"
  TtApp {} -> "app"
  -- containment-substrate Phase 2 Step 1b — the tier-2 cross-base formers route
  -- through tsKindFormer (split off to keep tsKind under the Fenel-bodied parser's
  -- per-decl token cap; a missing arm there falls to "other" ⇒ sound-but-coarse).
  _ -> tsKindFormer t

@label "type-subsumes: tsKindFormer"
@description "containment-substrate Phase 2 Step 1b — the tier-2 former tail of tsKind (split off for the per-decl token cap): TtUnion ⇒ \"union\", TtIntersect ⇒ \"intersect\", TtComplement ⇒ \"complement\", else \"other\". These surface the structural decider arms in containment.fenel (subset / empty / disjoint)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "structural-dispatch" "subtype" "containment"
@category "engine-internal"
tsKindFormer : (t: a) -> String
tsKindFormer t = case t of
  TtUnion {} -> "union"
  TtIntersect {} -> "intersect"
  TtComplement {} -> "complement"
  _ -> "other"

@label "type-subsumes: tsIsVar"
@description "structural-dispatch Phase 4a — is the marshalled type a TtVar (type variable)? Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "structural-dispatch" "subtype"
@category "engine-internal"
tsIsVar : (t: a) -> Bool
tsIsVar t = case t of
  TtVar -> True
  _ -> False

@label "type-subsumes: tsBase"
@description "structural-dispatch Phase 4a — the base type of a TtRefined (else passthrough). Internal accessor."
@tags "engine" "internal" "structural-dispatch" "subtype"
@category "engine-internal"
tsBase : (t: a) -> a
tsBase t = case t of
  TtRefined { base = b } -> b
  _ -> t

@label "type-subsumes: tsRefinedSet"
@description "structural-dispatch Phase 4a — the refinement SetExpr carried on a TtRefined (Phase-4a marshal extension); passed opaquely to set:decideSubset. Else passthrough. Internal accessor."
@tags "engine" "internal" "structural-dispatch" "subtype"
@category "engine-internal"
tsRefinedSet : (t: a) -> b
tsRefinedSet t = case t of
  TtRefined { set = s } -> s
  _ -> t

@label "type-subsumes: tsPure"
@description "structural-dispatch Phase 4a — the pure-ADT view of a TtOpaque (else passthrough). Internal accessor."
@tags "engine" "internal" "structural-dispatch" "subtype"
@category "engine-internal"
tsPure : (t: a) -> a
tsPure t = case t of
  TtOpaque { pure = p } -> p
  _ -> t

@label "type-subsumes: tsName"
@description "structural-dispatch Phase 4a — the name of a TtNamed (else \"\"). Internal accessor."
@tags "engine" "internal" "structural-dispatch" "subtype"
@category "engine-internal"
tsName : (t: a) -> String
tsName t = case t of
  TtNamed { name = n } -> n
  _ -> ""

@label "type-subsumes: tsMuBody"
@description "structural-dispatch Phase 4a — the body of a TtMu (else passthrough). Internal accessor."
@tags "engine" "internal" "structural-dispatch" "subtype"
@category "engine-internal"
tsMuBody : (t: a) -> a
tsMuBody t = case t of
  TtMu { body = b } -> b
  _ -> t

@label "type-subsumes: tsPhantom"
@description "structural-dispatch Phase 4a — the phantom type of a TtTagged (else passthrough). Internal accessor."
@tags "engine" "internal" "structural-dispatch" "subtype"
@category "engine-internal"
tsPhantom : (t: a) -> a
tsPhantom t = case t of
  TtTagged { phantom = p } -> p
  _ -> t

-- ── Maybe-shape congruence ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "type-subsumes: tsBothMaybe"
@description "structural-dispatch Phase 4a — are BOTH marshalled types Maybe-shaped variants (a Just+Nothing case pair)? Internal helper for tsSameKind's variant arm."
@tags "engine" "internal" "structural-dispatch" "subtype"
@category "engine-internal"
tsBothMaybe : (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Bool
tsBothMaybe have want =
  if tsIsMaybe have then tsIsMaybe want else False

@label "type-subsumes: tsIsMaybe"
@description "structural-dispatch Phase 4a — is the marshalled type a Maybe-shaped variant (cases include both Just and Nothing)? Reuses universe-views' hasCaseNamed. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "structural-dispatch" "subtype"
@category "engine-internal"
tsIsMaybe : (t: a) -> Bool
tsIsMaybe t = case t of
  TtVariant { cases = cs } ->
    if hasCaseNamed cs "Just" then hasCaseNamed cs "Nothing" else False
  _ -> False

@label "type-subsumes: tsMaybeInner"
@description "structural-dispatch Phase 4a — extract the inner (Just-field) type of a Maybe-shaped marshalled variant as Maybe TraversalType. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "structural-dispatch" "subtype"
@category "engine-internal"
tsMaybeInner : (t: a) -> Maybe b
tsMaybeInner t = case t of
  TtVariant { cases = cs } -> tsJustInner cs
  _ -> Nothing

@label "type-subsumes: tsJustInner"
@description "structural-dispatch Phase 4a — walk a variant's case list to the case named \"Just\" and return its first field's type (Maybe TraversalType). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "structural-dispatch" "subtype"
@category "engine-internal"
tsJustInner : (cs: a) -> Maybe b
tsJustInner cs = case head cs of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just c ->
    case c of
      TtVariantCase { name = n, fields = fs } ->
        if eq n "Just" then tsFirstFieldType fs
        else tsJustInnerRest cs
      _ -> tsJustInnerRest cs

@label "type-subsumes: tsJustInnerRest"
@description "structural-dispatch Phase 4a — tail recursion for tsJustInner. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "structural-dispatch" "subtype"
@category "engine-internal"
tsJustInnerRest : (cs: a) -> Maybe b
tsJustInnerRest cs = case tail cs of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just rest -> tsJustInner rest

@label "type-subsumes: tsFirstFieldType"
@description "structural-dispatch Phase 4a — the type of the first TtField in a field list (Maybe TraversalType). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "structural-dispatch" "subtype"
@category "engine-internal"
tsFirstFieldType : (fs: a) -> Maybe b
tsFirstFieldType fs = case head fs of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just f ->
    case f of
      TtField { type = ft } -> Just ft
      _ -> Nothing

-- ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- functionsMatchingReturn — the ⊆-arm universe-view the FunctionPicker consumes.
-- The ids of every fn whose marshalled `returnType` `typeSubsumes` the expected
-- type. The HEAVY sibling of Phase-3's LIGHT nominal `functionsReturning`.
-- ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "Functions matching return"
@description "structural-dispatch Phase 4a — the ⊆-arm universe-view `functionsMatchingReturn(expectedType)`: the ids of every function in the marshalled list whose return type `typeSubsumes` (is a subtype of) the expected type, matching by genuine subtype precision (refined leaves via the shipped set:decideSubset). The editor's FunctionPicker consumes this in-process to filter its candidate functions + constructors by the expected type — replacing the browser-side `typeMatches`. The HEAVY sibling of Phase-3's LIGHT nominal `functionsReturning`."
@tags "engine" "structural-dispatch" "universe-views" "subtype" "introspection"
functionsMatchingReturn : (expected: TraversalType) -> (fns: List a) -> List String
functionsMatchingReturn expected fns =
  functionsMatchingReturnFold expected fns []

@label "type-subsumes: functionsMatchingReturnFold"
@description "structural-dispatch Phase 4a — the head/tail fold behind functionsMatchingReturn: append `f.id` whenever `typeSubsumes f.returnType expected`. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "structural-dispatch" "universe-views" "subtype"
@category "engine-internal"
functionsMatchingReturnFold : (expected: a) -> (fns: List b) -> (acc: List String) -> List String
functionsMatchingReturnFold expected fns acc =
  case head fns of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just f ->
      let acc2 = if typeSubsumes f.returnType expected
                   then appendItem f.id acc
                   else acc
      case tail fns of
        Nothing -> acc2
        Just rest -> functionsMatchingReturnFold expected rest acc2
